From: John Merchant <john@johnmerchant.dev>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 19:12:37 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 13/14] mtd: rawnand: mxc: accept a lone wait for ready

nand_do_read_ops() calls nand_wait_readrdy() for chips with
NAND_NEED_READRDY, which all small-page chips have. That is an
operation of only a WAITRDY instruction, which none of mxc_nand's
parser patterns matched, so every page read of a small-page chip (the
i.MX21's 64 MiB Hynix on the Chumby Classic) warned in
nand_wait_readrdy(). The NFC waits for ready itself, so accept it and
do nothing.

Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01B1fN5Ee1gRFAS7tp8oLbvQ
---
 drivers/mtd/nand/raw/mxc_nand.c | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/mtd/nand/raw/mxc_nand.c b/drivers/mtd/nand/raw/mxc_nand.c
index 4d8b92e7e..03da610a0 100644
--- a/drivers/mtd/nand/raw/mxc_nand.c
+++ b/drivers/mtd/nand/raw/mxc_nand.c
@@ -1671,6 +1671,9 @@ static const struct nand_op_parser mxcnd_op_parser = NAND_OP_PARSER(
 			       NAND_OP_PARSER_PAT_DATA_OUT_ELEM(false, MAX_DATA_SIZE),
 			       NAND_OP_PARSER_PAT_CMD_ELEM(true),
 			       NAND_OP_PARSER_PAT_WAITRDY_ELEM(true)),
+	/* nand_wait_readrdy() on small-page chips */
+	NAND_OP_PARSER_PATTERN(mxcnd_do_exec_op,
+			       NAND_OP_PARSER_PAT_WAITRDY_ELEM(false)),
 	);
 
 static int mxcnd_exec_op(struct nand_chip *chip,
